{
  "strategy": "Locate the spoken mention of Cologne via ASR, then inspect frames at that exact utterance time to count the boats visible by the shore. This directly grounds both the temporal anchor and the visual count needed for the multiple-choice answer.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "tool": "asr",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "VIDEO_PATH",
        "start_time": null,
        "end_time": null
      },
      "purpose": "Find the transcript segment containing the phrase about discovering Cologne and obtain its timestamped speech interval.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tool": "frame_retriever",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "VIDEO_PATH",
        "query": null,
        "timestamps": [
          "<STEP_1:segments>"
        ],
        "num_frames": 3
      },
      "purpose": "Retrieve candidate frames around the ASR-identified Cologne mention so the shoreline scene at the narration moment can be visually inspected.",
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tool": "counter",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_2:frames>",
        "timestamp": null,
        "query": "boats moored by the shore",
        "exemplar_paths": null
      },
      "purpose": "Count the number of boats tied up along the shore in the candidate frames from the Cologne narration moment.",
      "depends_on": [2]
    }
  ],
  "refinement_instructions": "Build the trace from scratch. First, use the ASR output to identify the exact transcript segment containing the quote about Cologne; do not rely on any unrelated ASR segment by index unless its text matches the quote. Then use the retrieved frame timestamps aligned to that utterance to identify the correct frame-level scene during the mention. In the counter output, inspect per-frame results if available and choose the frame whose timestamp best matches the utterance interval from ASR; do not assume the first retrieved frame is correct. State the observed boat count directly from the counter evidence and map it to the answer option. If the ASR segment spans multiple frames with different visible counts, prefer the frame most centrally aligned with the spoken mention and mention that provenance explicitly in the rewritten trace."
}
